  "configuration_id": "config_037",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_025, acc=0.635) uses PCA_n2000 as the RNA encoder, and all completed experiments share this encoder. We have zero evidence about whether a learned encoder (SCVI) could improve on PCA in the multimodal pipeline. The other design axes (profile=multiprofile, aggregation=avgpool, image=ViT-L, fusion=weighted) are well-supported by the data. Question: config_037 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to SCVI_n200 while holding every other parameter at its best-known value, directly testing whether a deep generative RNA representation outperforms linear PCA in the multimodal fusion context. Why this is the best next experiment: The RNA encoder is the single largest unexplored design dimension, and its impact could be comparable to or exceed the profile-setting effect (~10%). Testing it in the strongest known configuration (rather than in a weaker RNA-only setting) gives the most decision-relevant information: if SCVI matches or beats PCA here, it opens a high-value branch; if it underperforms, we efficiently rule out that direction and consolidate on PCA. This maximizes information gain per limited experiment."
}

